\end{table}
\vspace{-0.15em}
\begin{alertblock}{Interpretation}
\scriptsize
The conclusion does not change as costs rise to 20 bps: the same OOS temporary and permanent winners remain selected in every universe. Higher costs reduce net returns, but the active alpha ranking is stable because benchmark rows receive the same cost convention.
\end{alertblock}
\remarkfoot{Alpha is net annualized geometric return minus the corresponding benchmark annualized return. Sources: \texttt{best\_by\_track\_index\_cost.csv}, \texttt{transaction\_cost\_robustness\_summary.csv}, and \texttt{transaction\_cost\_impact.csv}.}
\end{frame}

%==== 4b. Data findings =======================================================%

\begin{frame}{Turnover Effect}
\fontsize{5.1pt}{5.65pt}\selectfont
\textbf{Cost drag scales with annualized gross buy+sell turnover in the selected OOS winners}
\vspace{-0.25em}
\begin{table}[ht]
\centering
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{1.35pt}
\begin{tabular}{L{0.70cm}L{0.78cm}L{2.03cm}R{0.78cm}R{0.62cm}R{0.62cm}R{0.62cm}}
\toprule
Track & Univ. & Selected OOS winner & Turnover & Drag 5 & Drag 10 & Drag 20 \\
\midrule
Temp. & Total & AG Base; Youden 3yr & 10.4\% & 0.03pp & 0.05pp & 0.10pp \\
Temp. & Large & AG Base; Youden 3yr & 13.0\% & 0.03pp & 0.07pp & 0.13pp \\
Temp. & Mid & AG Base; FPR5 5yr & 105.9\% & 0.26pp & 0.53pp & 1.06pp \\
Temp. & Small & AG +VAE; Youden 3yr & 85.5\% & 0.21pp & 0.43pp & 0.85pp \\
Perm. & Total & AG +VAE; FPR5 perm. & 6.8\% & 0.02pp & 0.03pp & 0.07pp \\
Perm. & Large & AG +VAE; FPR5 perm. & 11.5\% & 0.03pp & 0.06pp & 0.12pp \\
Perm. & Mid & AG Base; FPR5 perm. & 106.2\% & 0.27pp & 0.53pp & 1.06pp \\
Perm. & Small & AG Latent; FPR3 perm. & 75.7\% & 0.19pp & 0.38pp & 0.76pp \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}
\vspace{-0.15em}
\begin{alertblock}{Practical read}
\scriptsize
Turnover is not just a nuisance metric: it is the direct multiplier for transaction-cost drag. Mid and Small Cap winners trade much more of the portfolio, so their 20 bps drag is visibly larger than Total or Large Cap, even though the winner ranking remains stable.
\end{alertblock}
\remarkfoot{Turnover is annualized gross buy+sell traded weight. Drag values use source-provided total transaction-cost return drag from \texttt{best\_by\_track\_index\_cost.csv}; cross-checks use \texttt{turnover\_summary.csv}, \texttt{winner\_turnover\_summary\_20bps.csv}, and \texttt{transaction\_cost\_impact.csv}.}
\end{frame}

%==== 4b. Data findings =======================================================%

\begin{frame}{Threshold Families and Turnover}
\fontsize{5.55pt}{6.1pt}\selectfont
\textbf{Final selected rules use finite lockouts for temporary CSI and stricter FPR cutoffs for permanent CSI}
\vspace{-0.25em}
\begin{table}[ht]
\centering
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{1.8pt}
\begin{tabular}{L{0.82cm}L{2.62cm}L{2.08cm}L{2.22cm}}
\toprule
Track & Final selected rule families & 20 bps family evidence & Turnover interpretation \\
\midrule
Temp. & Youden 3yr wins Total, Large, and Small; FPR5 5yr wins Mid. & Youden has the strongest mean best alpha at 20 bps: +0.35pp. & Finite 3--5yr lockouts let exclusions expire, limiting turnover outside Mid/Small. \\
Perm. & FPR5 permanent wins Total, Large, and Mid; FPR3 permanent wins Small. & FPR3/FPR5 lead at 20 bps: +0.35pp/+0.33pp; Youden averages -0.20pp. & Permanent removal needs stricter fixed-FPR gates; broad Youden exclusion over-removes names. \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}
\vspace{-0.1em}
\begin{table}[ht]
\centering
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{2.2pt}
\begin{tabular}{L{1.10cm}R{0.72cm}R{0.72cm}R{0.72cm}R{0.72cm}}
\toprule
Track & Total & Large & Mid & Small \\
\midrule
Temp. turnover & 10.4\% & 13.0\% & 105.9\% & 85.5\% \\
Perm. turnover & 6.8\% & 11.5\% & 106.2\% & 75.7\% \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}
\vspace{-0.15em}
\begin{alertblock}{Interpretation}
\scriptsize
The final rules are not arbitrary threshold-grid winners. Temporary CSI uses recoverable lockouts where the signal can age out; Permanent CSI uses narrower FPR cutoffs because permanent exclusion is absorbing and turnover/cost mistakes compound.
\end{alertblock}
\remarkfoot{Sources: \texttt{threshold\_family\_summary\_20bps.csv}, \texttt{winner\_turnover\_summary\_20bps.csv}, and \texttt{best\_by\_track\_index\_cost.csv}.}
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}{Sensitivity: Temporary CSI Main Run Versus C/M/T Grid}
\fontsize{5.45pt}{5.95pt}\selectfont
\begin{columns}[T,onlytextwidth]
\begin{column}{0.58\textwidth}
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{../../../../05_Documentation/09_Epics/AE-SENS-CHART_Sensitivity_Index_Charts/charts/chart1_sensitivity_stability_distribution.png}
\end{column}
\begin{column}{0.40\textwidth}
\textbf{Main-run comparison}
\vspace{-0.35em}
\begin{table}[ht]
\centering
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{1.25pt}
\begin{tabular}{L{0.72cm}R{0.40cm}R{0.58cm}R{0.58cm}R{0.88cm}}
\toprule
Univ. & Runs & Main & Median & Range \\
\midrule
Total & 24 & 0.06 & 0.10 & 0.02--0.23 \\
Large & 24 & 0.04 & 0.07 & 0.02--0.19 \\
Mid & 24 & 0.18 & 0.13 & 0.03--0.33 \\
Small & 24 & 0.38 & 0.18 & 0.03--0.66 \\
\bottomrule
