\end{table}
\vspace{-0.35em}
\scriptsize
Values are benchmark-relative geometric-return deltas in percentage points.
\vspace{0.1em}
\textbf{Robustness read.} Temporary-CSI sensitivity supports the main run as a defensible, non-outlier setting. Completed C/M/T runs remain positive across all four universes; the main run is below median in Total/Large and above median in Mid/Small.

\vspace{0.35em}
\textbf{Limit.} This sensitivity evidence is temporary CSI only. Three blocked partial C/M/T configurations are excluded, so the result supports stability of completed runs rather than an exhaustive permanent-CSI claim.
\end{column}
\end{columns}
