\begin{frame}{Appendix A19: Temporary CSI Sensitivity Detail}
\fontsize{5.55pt}{6.05pt}\selectfont
\textbf{Temporary-CSI sensitivity only: selected configurations, main-run comparison, and limits}
\vspace{-0.25em}
\begin{table}[ht]
\centering
\setlength{\tabcolsep}{1.6pt}
\begin{tabular}{L{1.35cm}L{1.55cm}R{0.65cm}R{0.65cm}R{0.65cm}R{0.65cm}R{1.00cm}L{0.95cm}}
\toprule
Role & Run ID & Pos. & Prev. & OOS AP & OOS AUC & 11C TM alpha & Status \\
\midrule
Composite & \texttt{C090\_M000\_T012} & 12,761 & 7.02\% & 0.557 & 0.920 & +0.169pp & complete \\
AP winner & \texttt{C060\_M000\_T012} & 31,596 & 17.49\% & 0.566 & 0.864 & +0.052pp & reused \\
11C winner & \texttt{C090\_M020\_T018} & 6,035 & 3.34\% & 0.274 & 0.911 & +0.226pp & complete \\
Baseline & \texttt{C080\_M020\_T018} & 8,517 & 4.74\% & 0.308 & 0.896 & +0.065pp & reused \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}
\vspace{-0.05em}
\begin{block}{Main comparison and stability}
\scriptsize
The accepted main run \texttt{C080\_M020\_T018} is the continuity baseline, not the top sensitivity setting. Across 24 completed/reused C/M/T runs, benchmark-relative index alpha remains positive in all four universes; sensitivity changes magnitude more than direction.
\end{block}
\vspace{-0.15em}
\begin{block}{Limits and transaction-cost overlay}
\scriptsize
The grid represents 27 temporary-CSI configurations: 24 are complete or reused, and three are \texttt{blocked\_partial}: \texttt{C080\_M000\_T012}, \texttt{C080\_M000\_T018}, and \texttt{C060\_M020\_T028}. The sensitivity evidence does not support permanent-CSI claims. In the accepted-label temporary index grid, 0/5/10/20 bps overlays do not change the winner set.
\end{block}
\remarkfoot{Sources: local \texttt{sensitivity\_cmt\_model\_summary.csv}; \texttt{sensitivity\_cmt\_index\_summary.csv}; \texttt{temporary\_index\_transaction\_cost\_lines.csv}; \texttt{temporary\_blocked\_config\_disclosure.csv}.}
\end{frame}

\begin{frame}{Appendix A20: CV Metrics Versus Index Alpha}
\fontsize{5.35pt}{5.85pt}\selectfont
\centering
\includegraphics[width=\linewidth,height=0.71\textheight,keepaspectratio]{../../../../05_Documentation/09_Epics/AE-PRES-QA-FIX_Final_Presentation_QA_Fixes/charts/slide48_cv_metrics_vs_cv_test_alpha.png}
\vspace{-0.35em}
\begin{itemize}
  \item CV-only AP/AUC/R@FPR3/R@FPR5 do not map cleanly into total-market alpha; AP is near zero against test alpha.
  \item Index performance is the realized result after thresholding, timing, universe weights, and returns, not a generic ML metric.
  \item The 11C source period is named \texttt{insample}; this slide labels it as in-sample/CV-proxy alpha.
\end{itemize}
\remarkfoot{Sources: \texttt{slide48\_cv\_metrics\_vs\_cv\_test\_alpha.png}; local \texttt{sensitivity\_cmt\_model\_summary.csv}; \texttt{combined\_11c\_performance.csv}; AE-PRES-QA-FIX-008 evidence.}
\end{frame}

